From 8606f8a0d8d67ae66ae0fdd65b103a2b5a0809f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: serlk <22211586+Serlk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 03:03:14 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Titan 2: AxSandbox: permission checks for state-changing
 calls

The ax_sandbox binder service did no caller checks at all; only the
service policy guarded it, and that lets platform, GMS, NFC and
Bluetooth apps in. Any of them could isolate an app or take it out of
isolation, change its scopes, gids and data isolation, lock, hide or
unlock any app, read and inject hidden notifications, or list every
locked, hidden and isolated app.

The binder interface is now a separate BinderService that checks the
caller and then delegates; system_server keeps calling the methods of
AxSandboxService directly, unchecked, since it calls them while serving
other apps.

- state changes, unlockApp, hidden notifications and the lists of all
  apps: system uid only (system_server, the Sandbox manager and
  AppLocker, both android.uid.system), run with a cleared identity
- promptUnlock, lock state of other apps, lock and session listeners:
  also STATUS_BAR_SERVICE (SystemUI and the recents launcher)
- queries about one package: the system or the package itself
  (SettingsProvider asks getSpoofedSetting with the reading app's
  identity and package)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
